cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Enterprise Structural Awareness"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: Loswin
    given-names: Nawder
abstract: >
  Enterprise Structural Awareness is a descriptive framework for introducing
  regime context, validity assumptions, and boundary semantics into existing
  enterprise IT systems using standards-based, non-intrusive approaches.
  The work focuses on interpretability, coherence, and long-term operational
  clarity without altering system behavior or control logic.
keywords:
  - enterprise systems
  - structural awareness
  - regime modeling
  - configuration management
  - operational clarity
